exports[`golden de DOM — Run and Debug (renderDebugPane / drawDbg) > sessão code: variante «clone» percorrida até ao fim (root cause) > feed-code-session 1`] = `
"<div class="dbg"><div class="dbg-feed" id="dbg-feed"><div class="dbg-focus">Now analysing: <b>the result</b></div><div class="df look"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--blue)">Looking at</span><div>Debugging <code>tokenize_emits_eof</code> on <code>lib.rs</code> as it is now (<code>for c in chars.clone()</code>). Breakpoints: line 10.</div></div><div class="df think"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--accent-hover)">Analysing</span><div><span class="dbg-ln">line 3</span> Entered <code>tokenize("12")</code> from the test <code>tokenize_emits_eof</code>, which expects the last token to be <code>Eof</code>. Three ways this fails: Eof never gets pushed, the digits are tokenized wrong, or the test expects the wrong thing. The only thing that decides Eof is whether <code>chars</code> is exhausted at line 10 — so <code>chars</code> is what I am watching.</div></div><div class="df think"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--accent-hover)">Analysing</span><div><span class="dbg-ln">line 4</span> <code>tokens</code> is empty and has not allocated yet. <code>chars</code> becomes a <code>Peekable</code> over <code>"12"</code>; its cursor sits before <code>'1'</code>.</div></div><div class="df think"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--accent-hover)">Analysing</span><div><span class="dbg-ln">line 5</span> The loop iterates over <code>chars.clone()</code>: a <b>copy</b> of the iterator. Everything the loop consumes comes out of the copy — the original <code>chars</code> will not move. That is the first thing I would flag; I will confirm it at line 10.</div></div><div class="df think"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--accent-hover)">Analysing</span><div><span class="dbg-ln">line 6</span> <code>c = '1'</code> is an ASCII digit, so it will be pushed.</div></div><div class="df think"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--accent-hover)">Analysing</span><div><span class="dbg-ln">line 7</span> <code>tokens</code> allocated on the first push: capacity 4 (Rust's minimum for small elements). <code>Token</code> is 4 bytes thanks to the niche in <code>char</code>.</div></div><div class="df think"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--accent-hover)">Analysing</span><div><span class="dbg-ln">line 6</span> Second character <code>'2'</code>. Note the variables: the <b>copy</b> is advancing, the original <code>chars</code> still says <code>next '1'</code>.</div></div><div class="df think"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--accent-hover)">Analysing</span><div><span class="dbg-ln">line 7</span> Both digits are in <code>tokens</code> — the digit handling is fine, so I am dropping that hypothesis.</div></div><div class="df evidence"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--yellow)">Evidence</span><div><span class="dbg-ln">line 10</span> Here it is. <code>chars.peek()</code> returns <code>Some('1')</code>: the original iterator was <b>never advanced</b>, because the loop consumed the copy. The condition is false, so <code>Eof</code> is skipped. This explains the test failure completely; the other two hypotheses are ruled out by what we saw.</div></div><div class="df think"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--accent-hover)">Analysing</span><div><span class="dbg-ln">line 13</span> Returns <code>[Num('1'), Num('2')]</code> — no <code>Eof</code>. The test will fail with <code>left: Some(Num('2')), right: Some(Eof)</code>.</div></div><div class="df root"><span class="dk" style="color:var(--red)">Root cause</span><div><b>Root cause found.</b> The compiler's suggestion fixed the <b>compile</b> error but changed the <b>behaviour</b>: cloning a <code>Peekable</code> gives the loop its own cursor, so the original never reaches the end and <code>peek()</code> keeps seeing <code>'1'</code>.<br><br><b>Fix:</b> lend the iterator instead of copying it — <code>for c in chars.by_ref()</code>. It compiles for the same reason the clone did (the loop no longer takes ownership), and it keeps a single cursor.<br><br><b>Lesson:</b> when <code>rustc</code> says “consider cloning”, ask whether you need a second value or just a second <i>use</i> of the same one. For iterators it is almost always the second.</div></div></div>
   <div class="dbg-side"><div class="dbg-t">Hypotheses</div><div class="hy"><div class="hy-h"><span>Eof is never pushed</span><b>97%</b></div><i><b style="width:97%;background:var(--red)"></b></i></div><div class="hy out"><div class="hy-h"><span>The test expects the wrong thing</span><b>2%</b></div><i><b style="width:2%;background:var(--fg-muted)"></b></i></div><div class="hy out"><div class="hy-h"><span>Digits are tokenized wrong</span><b>1%</b></div><i><b style="width:1%;background:var(--fg-muted)"></b></i></div>
   <div class="dbg-t">Next</div><button class="dbg-p">Apply the fix and re-run</button><button class="dbg-p">Explain this to me in depth</button></div></div>"
`;

